{
    "id": "art-4",
    "title": "Digital Doubles",
    "fullDescription": "This portfolio showcases the creation of over 20 digital doubles for various film productions, highlighting the intricate process of replicating actors and creatures with photorealistic accuracy. Starting with high-quality image sets from multiple angles, I employ photogeometry techniques to establish the foundational geometry. While photogeometry provides a strong base for measurements, capturing fine micro and even some medium-level details can be challenging. Therefore, the photogeometry serves as a precise guide for meticulous manual sculpting in ZBrush, where I refine the form and add lifelike details. The final stage involves detailed texturing to achieve a truly realistic digital representation that seamlessly integrates with live-action footage.",
    "client": "<a href='https://mainroadpost.com' target='_blank' class='client-link'>Main Road Post</a>",
    "date": "2015 - 2023",
    "tools": [
        "ZBrush",
        "3ds Max",
        "Substance Painter",
        "Photoshop"
    ],
    "role": "Digital Sculptor & VFX Artist",
